 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are recorded on the bundle at definition time, then replayed onto the app at registration.\n\n**1. Recording** (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`): `Bundle.attach_route_rule` doesn't touch the app. It calls `Bundle.record(...)` (line 224) with a lambda `lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...)`, which appends to `Bundle.deferred_functions`.\n\n**2. Registration**\n- `App.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `bundle.register(self, options)`.\n- `Bundle.register` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:273`):\n  - adds the bundle to `app.bundles`;\n  - builds a state via `Bundle.make_setup_state` (line 246), which returns a `BundleSetupState`;\n  - if the bundle has a static folder, calls `state.attach_route_rule` for the static route (line 324);\n  - runs each `deferred(state)` in `deferred_functions` (line 334);\n  - recurses into nested bundles, computing their combined `url_prefix`, `subdomain` and `name_prefix`.\n\n**3. Applying to the app** (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:87`): `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` does the following:\n- prepends `url_prefix` to the rule;\n- sets the subdomain;\n- merges `url_defaults`;\n- prefixes the endpoint with `name_prefix.name.`;\n- calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)`, which is `App.attach_route_rule` in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606` and adds the rule to the URL map.",
